## Original Content
Among Beatles connoisseurs, it’s fair game to claim anything from Rubber Soul to Abbey Road as one’s favorite album. But even within that span of the catalog, a hierarchy of acclaim exists, and that hierarchy has been rearranged over the decades. The ecstatic reception of Sgt. Pepper’s Lonely Hearts Club Band lasted&#160;at least a decade. [&#8230;]

## Summary
This article explores the creation and enduring legacy of the Beatles' album Revolver, released 60 years ago. It discusses the evolving hierarchy of acclaim among the Beatles' albums, with Sgt. Pepper’s Lonely Hearts Club Band notably receiving ecstatic reception that lasted for years.

## Key Points
- Revolver is considered one of the Beatles' most acclaimed albums.
- The hierarchy of praise among Beatles albums has shifted over decades.
- Sgt. Pepper’s Lonely Hearts Club Band had a significant and lasting impact on reception.
- The article commemorates the 60th anniversary of Revolver's release.


